1. INR\ 140 mmHg, diastolic blood pressure \> 90 mmHg), with classⅡand above coronary heart disease and arrhythmia (including QTc lengthened men \> 450 ms, women \> 470 ms) and cardiac insufficiency; 3. A variety of factors influencing oral drugs (such as unable to swallow, nausea, vomiting, chronic diarrhea and intestinal obstruction, etc.); 4. Patients with tendency of gastrointestinal bleeding, including the following;

