, bleeding tendency or receiving thrombolytic or anticoagulant therapy; Note: On the premise that the international normalized ratio (INR) of prothrombin time is ≤1.5, the use of low-dose heparin (daily dosage of 0.6-12,000 U for adults) or low-dose aspirin (daily dosage of ≤ 100 U) is allowed for prophylactic purposes. mg); 10. Patients with any severe and/or uncontrolled disease, including:

